# Real Claude CLI 2.1.310 E2E: forced parent-model inheritance

Harness: `e2e_models.py` (+ `console_agent.py`, reused `console_driver.py`/`shot_title.ps1` from 2026/10/16).
Fake loopback Anthropic Messages server returns deterministic Agent tool_use; children are identified by an
`E2ECHILD-<tag>` marker in their first user turn. Only model/tool-schema/marker metadata is kept.
Summary: `comparison.json`. Environment: projection from source `ciel_runtime.env_vars()` (no hand-set model env),
all inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_/CLAUDE*/ANTHROPIC*/CODEX*/OPENAI* removed, fresh HOME/config/workspace/ports, egress sentinel proxy.

## Child model on the wire (gateway-observed)

| case | plain | Agent model=haiku | Agent model=sonnet | definition model: haiku | --model fake-parent-b | named teammate | new teammate after /model fake-parent-b |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| old env (SUBAGENT_MODEL=parent, no FORCE) direct `e2e-old-bbeb99` | fake-parent-a | fake-haiku | fake-sonnet | fake-haiku | fake-parent-a (stale) | fake-parent-a | not run |
| fixed direct `e2e-fixed-ea293e`, `e2e-switch-21da1f` | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-b | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-b |
| fixed routed `e2e-routed-ef077c`, `e2e-routedswitch-82ff03` | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-b | fake-parent-a | fake-parent-b |

- Fixed projection (direct and routed) recorded `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=inherit` and `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL_FORCE=1`
  while provider config carried `subagent_model=fake-haiku` (ignored). Direct keeps `inherit` (not mapped to an upstream id).
- Fixed Agent tool schema sent by the CLI has no `model` property; CLI 2.1.310 still accepted the explicit haiku/sonnet
  inputs (no validation error in transcript tool_results) and ran the child on the parent model. No retry was needed.
- `inherit` never appeared as a request model in any run (`inherit_on_wire=false`).
- Named teammates returned teammate-spawned metadata (agent teams enabled via `CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1`).

## Screenshots (actual Windows Terminal Claude Code windows, PrintWindow)
`screenshot-fixed-switched.png`, `screenshot-routed-switched.png` (teammate before and after /model),
`screenshot-fixed-named.png`, `screenshot-old-named.png`. Matching console text: each run `screen-latest.txt`.

## Safety
Live routers 9385/9464/9489/9505/9524 /health PIDs identical before/after in every run. Only harness-owned PIDs were killed.
Egress sentinel saw only blocked CONNECTs to downloads.claude.ai and github.com (CLI non-model traffic); no model request left loopback.

## Limitations
See `comparison.json.limitations`. Notably: old case is an env control on the generated projection, not a HEAD launcher run;
direct cases call the source projection with a LaunchDataPath and start claude.exe directly (no gateway discovery);
routed cases record router-forwarded upstream model, not the literal CLI->router model string; superseded attempts retained.
